``` SR-01 | Which User's Search Is Eating Memory and CPU
    Splunk Administrator Field Manual - Gaurav Malik

    Use case: The search head or the indexers are pinned on memory or CPU and
    splunkd is slow to respond; identify the searches, users, and apps
    consuming the most resources right now and over the last few hours.
    Run on: SH, with indexer _introspection forwarded. Indexers record the
    remote half of each search under the same sid, so totals cover the whole
    search.
    Query: Main query
```
index=_introspection sourcetype=splunk_resource_usage component=PerProcess
    data.search_props.sid=* earliest=-4h
| eval sid='data.search_props.sid', user='data.search_props.user',
       app='data.search_props.app', label='data.search_props.label',
       search_type='data.search_props.type', role='data.search_props.role',
       mem_mb='data.mem_used', cpu_pct='data.pct_cpu'
| stats max(mem_mb) as peak_mem_mb max(cpu_pct) as peak_cpu_pct
        latest(_time) as last_seen
        by sid host role user app label search_type
| stats sum(peak_mem_mb) as total_peak_mem_mb
        max(peak_cpu_pct) as worst_host_cpu_pct
        dc(host) as hosts values(role) as roles latest(last_seen) as last_seen
        by sid user app label search_type
| eval total_peak_mem_gb=round(total_peak_mem_mb / 1024, 2),
       running_now=if(now() - last_seen < 120, "YES", "no")
| convert ctime(last_seen)
| sort - total_peak_mem_mb
| head 25
| table sid user app search_type label running_now total_peak_mem_gb
        worst_host_cpu_pct hosts roles last_seen
